From 2692e2ab6ae64cfc5b23152196d8afdcc205e8b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:54:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Offer the depth options for a video that carries a depth map,
 kept for the file; write the size of the views and refuse what is not laced

The 3D Video Settings window shows the options of drawing the views of a picture and its depth map (libstereo-layer's
DepthControls, the same in every player) for a video that carries a depth map. The set is the library's, with its measured
default; the choice is kept for the file in dragonplayerrc, group StereoVideo, like the swap, and is no entry at the default. The
global depth keys of the 3DVideo group are gone.

Saving the correction: a half or full size choice that the shape of the video does not give is written into Matroska and WebM
as DisplayWidth and DisplayHeight (RFC 9559 18.10) and refused for MP4, which has no field; a frame sequential or block laced
layout is refused unless the file's blocks are laced (StereoMode 13 and 14).

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
(cherry picked from commit 42d05441da612548f55704c1eecb8d138a7ce499)
